### ============================================================
### Admin: Reports — "Report a problem" from the detail pages
### (#4399, #5603, #5308)
###
### The queue /fix-events works through, resolving a subject's
### reports (which deletes them and leaves each reporter a note
### under the bell), and the flag that withdraws reporting from
### an account that abuses the form (#5604).
### ============================================================

### The open reports, one entry per event, act, promoter or venue
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/reports
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Resolve every report on one subject: kind and id from the list, outcome fixed or unchanged, reply optional
POST {{importer-host}}/api/admin/reports/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "kind": "venues",
  "id": 1,
  "outcome": "unchanged",
  "reply": "The address on the page is the venue's own."
}

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Every account, oldest first, with its report flag
GET {{importer-host}}/api/admin/accounts
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("status is 200", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Withdraw reporting from an account (enabled: true gives it back)
PUT {{importer-host}}/api/admin/accounts/can-report
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "operator@example.de", "enabled": false }

> {%
    client.test("status is 204", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 204, "Expected 204 but got " + response.status);
    });
%}

### Lift the cap of 200 open reports for an account (exempt: false restores it)
PUT {{importer-host}}/api/admin/accounts/report-cap-exempt
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "operator@example.de", "exempt": true }
